  "defect": "03b names its calibration set `nte` and fits the threshold on it, so every reported specificity is within-calibration-set. No script in src/ does a three-way negative split",
  "verdict": "THE ESTIMATOR, NOT THE MODEL. The out-of-sample false-positive rate falls inside the order-statistic bracket at 6 of 6 calibration sizes, and at the smallest it is 8.64% against a stated 5%, 1.7x nominal, with single splits reaching 36.7%. At 4 of 6 sizes the bracket's LOWER edge already exceeds nominal, so 5% is not an achievable rate at those sample sizes by any order statistic. The conformal threshold delivers its guarantee at every size, so the fix is arithmetic. Report a finite-sample bound, not an interpolated point estimate"
}